# .templatesyncignore — files an APPLICATION created from this template OWNS.
#
# Same syntax as .gitignore. The weekly template-sync workflow
# (devantler-tech/.github .github/workflows/template-sync.yaml, using
# AndreasAugustin/actions-template-sync) is skipped in this template repo itself
# and runs in every application created from it — opening a PR that brings template
# changes downstream. It only ever touches files that exist in this template, and
# it SKIPS anything matched here, so an application lists the files it has tailored
# and they are never clobbered by an upstream sync.
#
# Everything NOT listed here is TEMPLATE-OWNED shared plumbing kept current in
# every application by template-sync — change those upstream in
# devantler-tech/application-template, never by editing them in an application.
# Template-owned files: .github/workflows/{release,template-sync,stale-issues,codeql,lint}.yaml,
# .github/mega-linter.base.yml, .coderabbit.yaml, .markdownlint.json, .yamllint.yml, CLAUDE.md,
# docs/REFERENCE.md, zizmor.yml and, for a platform tenant, .github/workflows/cd.yaml, renovate.json,
# scripts/workflow-caller-pin-contract.test.sh, scripts/publish-pin-approved.sh
# (+ its test) and the scripts/fixtures/own-publisher.yaml they read. Where a
# shared file has an app-owned overlay (.mega-linter.yml
# extends .github/mega-linter.base.yml; codeql.yaml reads
# .github/codeql/codeql-config.yml), change the overlay to diverge, not the shared
# file. An application scaffolded without --tenancy lists the tenant files below, so
# they never come back.

# --- Identity & docs (tenant-specific) ---
AGENTS.md
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
.github/CODEOWNERS
.claude/skills/maintain/SKILL.md

# --- CI / release / dependency config the tenant tailors to its stack ---
.github/workflows/ci.yaml
.github/dependabot.yml
.releaserc
.gitignore

# --- The application's overlays on shared configuration ---
.mega-linter.yml
.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml

# --- The tenant's own application ---
# deploy/ holds the example app's Kustomize manifests; a tenant replaces them with
# its real app (renamed in one shot by scripts/rename-placeholders.sh), so the whole
# directory is tenant-owned. The Dockerfile is the placeholder app build to swap out.
deploy/
Dockerfile

# --- Scaffolding machinery (template-only; dead code in a live tenant) ---
# These exist to rename placeholders when a NEW repo is created from this
# template ("use this template" copies everything, so scaffolding still arrives
# at creation time). A scaffolded tenant never runs them again — ignoring them
# stops template-sync (re-)introducing them downstream, so a tenant that still
# carries them can delete them and they stay gone.
scripts/rename-placeholders.sh
scripts/rename-placeholders.test.sh
scripts/agent-instructions.test.sh
scripts/workflow-caller-contract.test.sh
scripts/tenant-ci-contract.test.sh
scripts/pod-security-admission.test.sh
scripts/pod-security-admission-contract.test.sh
scripts/tenant-rbac.test.sh
scripts/tenant-rbac-contract.test.sh
scripts/platform-tenant-envelope.test.sh
scripts/platform-tenant-envelope-contract.test.sh
scripts/platform-network-floor.test.sh
scripts/platform-network-floor-contract.test.sh
scripts/platform-vpa-floor.test.sh
scripts/platform-vpa-floor-contract.test.sh
.github/workflows/validate-scaffold.yaml

# --- The scaffold and its stacks (template-only; scripts/scaffold.sh removes them) ---
# stacks/ holds the Go and .NET sources the scaffold copies once. After that the
# copied files are the application's own, so nothing under stacks/ ever syncs.
stacks/
scripts/scaffold.sh
scripts/scaffold.test.sh
.github/workflows/validate-stacks.yaml

# --- This ignore-list itself (the tenant curates its own ownership) ---
# The tenant's copy is never overwritten, but each sync ADDS the entries of this
# template's list that the tenant's copy lacks, so an exclusion added here reaches
# tenants created before it. A tenant's own entries are kept. To receive a file
# this list excludes, a tenant adds the line `!<entry>` (for example
# `!.github/CODEOWNERS`) to its own copy, and that one entry is not added.
.templatesyncignore
